WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.832
Hey!

2
00:00:01.575 --> 00:00:03.845
Is the bookshelf left or right of the laptop?

3
00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:05.620
Hmm, let me see.

4
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:07.832
Aha!

5
00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:09.595
The bookshelf is on the right.

6
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.182
Faster reasoning.

7
00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:12.143
Less waiting.

8
00:00:13.332 --> 00:00:15.291
Four approaches to spatial reasoning.

9
00:00:15.688 --> 00:00:18.909
Vanilla models use no explicit geometry prior.

10
00:00:19.306 --> 00:00:22.022
Co-encoders add a runtime geometry encoder.

11
00:00:22.431 --> 00:00:24.101
Distillation learns from a teacher.

12
00:00:24.498 --> 00:00:29.847
GeoThinker-F predicts useful priors internally, then fuses selectively.

13
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.633
Geo Thinker gains spatial priors from an extra geometry encoder.

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.633
GeoThinker-F predicts those priors from within,

15
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:41.100
then fuses them.

16
00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:42.933
The benefit, with less waiting.

17
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.000
Lightweight heads read intermediate states.

18
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.133
During training,

19
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.233
an offline teacher supervises geometry,

20
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.033
while next-frame visual features supervise semantic prediction.

21
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.667
Gated fusion injects these priors into selected intermediate layers.

22
00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:03.000
At inference, the extra 3D encoder is gone.

23
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.300
On V S I Bench,

24
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.333
GeoThinker-F reaches seventy point four among leading spatial models.

25
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.733
With token compression on both models,

26
00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:17.467
inference is 3.6 times faster than Geo Thinker.

27
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.100
Geometry from a teacher, predicted from within.

28
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.533
GeoThinker-F.
